   "date": "2023-10-28T14:35:30Z",
   "subject": "is.na() returns a scalar or vector?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Dear NIMBLE developers,</div><div><br></div><div>I ran into a question about the behavior of the &quot;<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863055000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Ms_oezvW_iS5A_4O4mxTB\">is.na</a>&quot; function on p.135 of the documentation:</div><div><br></div><div>library(&quot;nimble&quot;)<br><br>is_na &lt;- nimbleFunction(<br>  run = function(x = double(1)) {<br>    if (<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863055000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Ms_oezvW_iS5A_4O4mxTB\">is.na</a>(x)){ <br>      print(x)<br>    }<br>    returnType(double(1))<br>    return(x)<br>  })<br>assign(&#39;is_na&#39;, is_na, envir = .GlobalEnv)<br>is_na_c = compileNimble(is_na)<br>x = c(NA,1,1)<br>is_na_c(x)<br>is_na(x)<br></div><div><br></div><div>The uncompiled version cannot run it because &quot;\r\n\r\n<span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(222,222,222);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(0,0,0);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(231,140,69)\">Error in if (<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863055000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Ms_oezvW_iS5A_4O4mxTB\">is.na</a>(x)) { : the condition has length &gt; 1</span></span></span>\r\n\r\n&quot;. When compiling it by nimbleModel(), it also returned this error but continued to proceed. <br></div><div><br></div><div>In the compiled version, it seems that the <a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863055000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Ms_oezvW_iS5A_4O4mxTB\">is.na</a>() accepts a vector and returns a scalar. I think its behavior is different from the <a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863055000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Ms_oezvW_iS5A_4O4mxTB\">is.na</a>() in base R. <br></div><div><br></div><div>I wonder:</div><div>1. How to avoid the error above when compiling it by nimbleModel(). Just ignore it?\r\n\r\n</div><div>2. What is the correct way to use <a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863055000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Ms_oezvW_iS5A_4O4mxTB\">is.na</a>() in the nimbleFunction?<br><br>Thanks a lot!</div><div>Keith<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rZQfuyfMBAAJ",
   "from": "Chris Paciorek",
   "author": "d78486bfff620d81",
   "date": "2023-11-01T15:18:43Z",
   "subject": "Re: is.na() returns a scalar or vector?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Keith,<div><br></div><div>Yes, <a href=\"https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-RCfunctions.html#basic-operations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-RCfunctions.html%23basic-operations&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863056000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2fN7jpNjd5pmzcHEYeuBZB\">here in the nimble manual</a> we imply that  `<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_NRIOeH2rilleO2L88Nle\">is.na</a>` should take in an array and return an array of the same size, as you were expecting, since we indicate it </div><div>behaves like its R counterpart.</div><div><br></div><div>In reality it returns a scalar and behaves like `any(<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_NRIOeH2rilleO2L88Nle\">is.na</a>(x))`.  In looking back through our issues we have an <a href=\"https://github.com/nimble-dev/nimble/issues/987\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/nimble-dev/nimble/issues/987&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1bwv9tf6fSBJMnKpQELbBA\">open issue</a> to address this but have (sloppily)</div><div>never actually done so.</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ll put it on our list to try to deal with for the next release.</div><div><div><br></div><div>As a work-around, you can use `<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_NRIOeH2rilleO2L88Nle\">is.na</a>` element-wise as illustrated as follows.</div><div><br></div><div>```</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>is_na &lt;- nimbleFunction(<br>    run = function(x = double(1)) {</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>        n = length(x)<br>        out = logical(length=n)<br>        returnType(logical(1))<br>        for(i in 1:n)<br>            out[i] = <a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_NRIOeH2rilleO2L88Nle\">is.na</a>(x[i])<br>        return(out)<br>   })<br>c_is_na &lt;- compileNimble(is_na)<br><div>```</div></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Sat, Oct 28, 2023 at 7:35 AM Keith Lau &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">genw...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Dear NIMBLE developers,</div><div><br></div><div>I ran into a question about the behavior of the &quot;<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_NRIOeH2rilleO2L88Nle\">is.na</a>&quot; function on p.135 of the documentation:</div><div><br></div><div>library(&quot;nimble&quot;)<br><br>is_na &lt;- nimbleFunction(<br>  run = function(x = double(1)) {<br>    if (<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_NRIOeH2rilleO2L88Nle\">is.na</a>(x)){ <br>      print(x)<br>    }<br>    returnType(double(1))<br>    return(x)<br>  })<br>assign(&#39;is_na&#39;, is_na, envir = .GlobalEnv)<br>is_na_c = compileNimble(is_na)<br>x = c(NA,1,1)<br>is_na_c(x)<br>is_na(x)<br></div><div><br></div><div>The uncompiled version cannot run it because &quot;\r\n\r\n<span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(222,222,222);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(0,0,0);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"color:rgb(231,140,69)\">Error in if (<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_NRIOeH2rilleO2L88Nle\">is.na</a>(x)) { : the condition has length &gt; 1</span></span></span>\r\n\r\n&quot;. When compiling it by nimbleModel(), it also returned this error but continued to proceed. <br></div><div><br></div><div>In the compiled version, it seems that the <a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_NRIOeH2rilleO2L88Nle\">is.na</a>() accepts a vector and returns a scalar. I think its behavior is different from the <a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_NRIOeH2rilleO2L88Nle\">is.na</a>() in base R. <br></div><div><br></div><div>I wonder:</div><div>1. How to avoid the error above when compiling it by nimbleModel(). Just ignore it?\r\n\r\n</div><div>2. What is the correct way to use <a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475863057000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_NRIOeH2rilleO2L88Nle\">is.na</a>() in the nimbleFunction?<br><br>Thanks a lot!</div><div>Keith<br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
    ],
